{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"golden-busied-nag","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from nonblack-brigandish-guillemot: its closing plan review raised this as an advisory finding. After ADR 0125, rebar checks op-certs for validity only unless the verifying environment lists the keys it trusts in `verify.trusted_opcert_keys`. ADR 0125 says that list belongs to each environment's own configuration, not the repository.\n\nNothing enforces that. `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` is an ordinary `[verify]` key (`src/rebar/_config_sections.py:83`). No code restricts which config layer may set it; a search of `src/rebar/_config*.py` finds no repository-scope restriction for any key. The op-cert gate resolves its configuration through the repository root, so a committed `rebar.toml` that sets the key is read like any other layer. A change under review could add a key to that file and widen the trust list of the very gate that checks it.\n\nUnverified: whether the CI gate's environment-variable list overrides or merges with a repository-level list. The fix depends on the answer, so the first step is a test that sets both and records which wins.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test records how `verify.trusted_opcert_keys` resolves when both a committed `rebar.toml` and the environment set it.\n- [ ] A committed `rebar.toml` cannot add a key to the trust list the op-cert gate uses, shown by a test that tries it.\n- [ ] No config key, env var or flag is added by the fix.","id":"eca7-e5b5-7640-403f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"A committed rebar.toml can widen the op-cert gate's trust list"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795213805057892001,"uuid":"b2e35a1f-25da-41a6-bc85-79c3c3b216c8"}